grep -rn 'our $VERSION' lib bin: all 21 modules under lib/ carry our $VERSION = 0.001; bin/mcp-hub carries none. Per skill getty-perl-release-author-getty: every file under lib/ and bin/ needs its own our $VERSION, else it ships versionless. dzil build still succeeds, and PodWeaver injects '=head1 VERSION / version 0.001' into bin/mcp-hub's POD from the dist version, but the script itself has no $VERSION variable, unlike every lib/ module. Not a build breaker, but a house-convention violation worth a one-line fix: add our $VERSION = '0.001'; under the ABSTRACT line.

2026-09-16 16:47 Fixed: added our $VERSION = '0.001'; to bin/mcp-hub under the # ABSTRACT line (before the first use), matching the lib/ modules. prove -lr t/ green (82 tests). NOT committed - main agent coordinates git.
